#. front matter: title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:2 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:5
msgid "3. Comparisons, logic, conditions and loops"
msgstr "3. Сравнения, логика, условия и loops"

#. html
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:8
msgid "<span>Session 3</span><span>practice: <code>03-conditions-and-loops/</code> in the homework repository</span>"
msgstr "<span>Занятие 3</span><span>упражнения: <code>03-conditions-and-loops/</code> в homework repository</span>"

#. html
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:9
msgid "<span><a href=\"../example-document\"><code>doc</code>: the example JSON document</a></span>"
msgstr "<span><a href=\"../example-document\"><code>doc</code>: примерният JSON документ</a></span>"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:12
msgid "**Today you will learn to:**"
msgstr "**Днес ще се научите да:**"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:14
msgid "compare values with `===`, `!==`, `<`, `>=` ... and avoid the traps of `==`;"
msgstr "сравнявате стойности с `===`, `!==`, `<`, `>=` ... и да избягвате капаните на `==`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:15
msgid "understand why `\"4.10\" < \"4.2\"` is `true`, and what that means for versions;"
msgstr "разбирате защо `\"4.10\" < \"4.2\"` е `true` и какво означава това за версиите;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:16
msgid "combine conditions with `&&`, `||` and `!`;"
msgstr "комбинирате условия с `&&`, `||` и `!`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:17
msgid "know which values are *truthy* and *falsy*, and give defaults with `||` and `??`;"
msgstr "знаете кои стойности са *truthy* и *falsy* и да задавате стойности по подразбиране с `||` и `??`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:18
msgid "make decisions with `if` / `else`, `switch` and the ternary operator `? :`;"
msgstr "вземате решения с `if` / `else`, `switch` и тернарния оператор `? :`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:19
msgid "stop a rule early when data is missing (a *guard clause*);"
msgstr "спирате правилото рано, когато липсват данни (*guard clause*);"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:20
msgid "repeat work with `for`, `while` and `do...while`, and control loops with `break` and `continue`;"
msgstr "повтаряте действия с `for`, `while` и `do...while` и да управлявате loops с `break` и `continue`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:22
msgid "read existing rules written in an older style (`var`, `==`, `== false`)."
msgstr "четете съществуващи правила, написани в по-стар стил (`var`, `==`, `== false`)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:24
msgid "Where this fits in the sample check rule - after today you can read and write all of it. Every part uses one of today's topics - the number in the comment is the section of this lecture:"
msgstr "Къде е мястото на тази тема в примерното правило за проверка - след днешното занятие можете да го четете и пишете цялото. Всяка част използва някоя от днешните теми - числото в коментара е разделът от тази лекция:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:79
msgid "`versionBelow(a, b)` is a ready-made helper for now - we write our own in session 5."
msgstr "`versionBelow(a, b)` засега е готова helper функция - собствена ще напишем в занятие 5."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:81
msgid "`?.` (optional chaining) is a preview: it stops at a missing level instead of throwing an error. More in section 5 and in session 6."
msgstr "`?.` (optional chaining) е поглед напред: спира при липсващо ниво, вместо да хвърли грешка. Повече в раздел 5 и в занятие 6."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:84
msgid "Almost every rule is a chain of decisions like these: \"is the data there?\", \"is it the right model?\", \"is the firmware too old?\". Getting the conditions exactly right is the most important skill in rule writing."
msgstr "Почти всяко правило е верига от решения като тези: \"има ли данни?\", \"това ли е моделът?\", \"твърде стар ли е firmware-ът?\". Точните условия са най-важното умение при писането на правила."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:88
msgid "1. Comparison operators"
msgstr "1. Оператори за сравнение"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:90
msgid "A comparison asks a question about two values. The answer is **always a boolean**: `true` or `false`."
msgstr "Сравнението задава въпрос за две стойности. Отговорът е **винаги boolean**: `true` или `false`."

